// Standalone regression test for the os.shell timeout hint.
//
// Without Full Disk Access, a shell command that touches a TCC-protected path
// does NOT fail fast — TCC raises a consent prompt against Owletto and, on an
// unattended Mac, nobody answers. The child blocks until SIGTERM, so the caller
// sees `timed_out: true` with partial stdout and no reason. Measured on the Mac
// mini 2026-07-31 (run 818316): a probe read $HOME, ~/Code, /tmp and /usr/bin,
// then stalled on ~/Desktop and burned its entire 30s budget.
//
// The bare timeout reads as "slow command", which sends callers to raise
// timeout_ms — the one fix that cannot help. The hint has to fire exactly when
// FDA is absent AND the run timed out, and stay silent otherwise: a hint on a
// successful run, or on a machine that HAS full disk access, is a false alarm
// that would teach agents to ignore it.
//
//   swiftc apps/mac/Owletto/LobuClient.swift \
//          apps/mac/Owletto/DeviceConnectorManifests.swift \
//          apps/mac/Owletto/MacShellActionService.swift \
//          apps/mac/Tests/ShellTimeoutHintTests.swift -o /tmp/shell-timeout-hint-test \
//   && /tmp/shell-timeout-hint-test

